   "id": 615056,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "After the submission of the Constitution to the states for ratification, James Madison’s greatest concern grew from",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1168196,
     "content_html": "his fear of the growing divide between the North and South"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168195,
     "content_html": "the endless debate over the need for a bill of rights"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168197,
     "content_html": "the strength of resistance to the Constitution expressed by the Anti-Federalists"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168194,
     "content_html": "the passage of tax bills that would disproportionately harm the small states"
    }
   ],
